<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Puts HemophageWarcasket.JobGiver_HemohunterDismember in the humanlike think tree, where a
    pilot in a hemohunter mental state gets the pads' strike from it in place of that
    state's bite. The giver's header has the rules.

    Core's Humanlike tree runs its mental state nodes and then the trees tagged
    Humanlike_PostMentalState (ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag, highest insertPriority first, the
    first valid job winning; 1.6 and 1.7), which is where a mod's own mental state gets its
    jobs: Vanilla Races Expanded - Sanguophage gives its hemohunter's bite there at priority
    100. insertPriority 101 asks this giver first.

    The states are the ability's DismemberExtension.hemohunterStates, which this tree leaves
    empty: the def stands in the main tree because it names no other mod's def, and does
    nothing until a compat root lists a state
    (1.6/Mods/VanillaRacesExpandedSanguophage/Patches/DismemberFeeding.xml).
  -->
  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>HPWC_HemohunterDismember</defName>
    <insertTag>Humanlike_PostMentalState</insertTag>
    <insertPriority>101</insertPriority>
    <thinkRoot Class="HemophageWarcasket.JobGiver_HemohunterDismember" />
  </ThinkTreeDef>
</Defs>
